      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T15:35:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think switching from area to component wise checks diverges from the legacy behavior.  Is this needed/intentional?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 155,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "fc7c537c08f34d4de19bba4396049e31973b4f3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "346aa5b0_47afccbe",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_ico/decoder/impl/SkIcoRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 156,
      "author": {
        "id": 4159917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T21:52:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is intentional. Unlike the legacy `SkIcoCodec`, the Rust codec exposes each ICO entry through `FrameInfo`, and `fFrameRect` is required to be contained by `SkCodec::dimensions()`. Selecting one entry by area can violate that invariant for mixed-aspect entries—for example, neither 256x16 nor 32x32 contains the other. Taking the maximum width and height independently gives a 256x32 canvas that contains both frame rectangles. For the normal square ICO case this is equivalent to selecting the largest-area entry. I added a comment documenting the reason for the divergence.\n\nAs Lukasz pointed in this comment (https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1373378/comment/f3c4b712_0ccec5a6/) moving away from the frames would not work with current base class used from blink for Skia rust Codecs, so I revisited the suggested approach: \n\n```\n\"Maybe the animation-frames-based-decoding-API is okay as long as there is also additional API for finding the right frame index? Maybe the root problem in the previous CL discussion wasn\u0027t the decoding API, but using the decoding API for selecting the frame to decode?\"\n```",
      "parentUuid": "946a2fb0_54befd4d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 155,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "fc7c537c08f34d4de19bba4396049e31973b4f3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
