      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T15:35:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`SkEncodedInfo::VerifyColor`, which is called from the factory, contains some [assertions](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/include/private/SkEncodedInfo.h;drc\u003dd2b9e48baf1697760afc1dc8ea3ad40110b8cacc;l\u003d193) that look like we may break here.  E.g. if we\u0027re always overriding alpha type with kUnpremul, we can end up with something like kGray/kUnpremul which will trigger.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 323,
        "startChar": 68,
        "endLine": 323,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "fc7c537c08f34d4de19bba4396049e31973b4f3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f112f06e_4e2b33d9",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_ico/decoder/impl/SkIcoRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 323,
      "author": {
        "id": 4159917
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T21:52:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch. Preserving the color model while forcing `kUnpremul_Alpha` can create invalid `SkEncodedInfo` combinations such as gray/unpremul. \n\nWith Chromium CL 8471969 allocating native-sized frame buffers, this defensive top-level alpha rewrite is no longer needed. I removed it so maxInfo retains the embedded codec’s valid color/alpha combination.",
      "parentUuid": "03a99200_ebf68359",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 323,
        "startChar": 68,
        "endLine": 323,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "fc7c537c08f34d4de19bba4396049e31973b4f3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f99b331d_ed061542",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_ico/decoder/impl/SkIcoRustCodec.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T15:35:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mucking with alpha type at this level (also in `MakeFromStream`) seems iffy: IIUC, we are doing this defensively, for clients that may pass in buffers with padding.  But that hurts clients which are well behaved and size their buffers appropriately.\n\nCan we delegate this logic to clients instead? They should be able to tell if they are using a larger buffer than needed for a frame, and can tweak the alpha type themselves, only when needed.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 161,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 163,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "fc7c537c08f34d4de19bba4396049e31973b4f3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
